      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define fraud indicators, escalation rules, and incident logging approach.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Let's move on to T4: fraud detection. I've started a draft guideline A4 with a list of common fraud indicators, like consistent round-number invoices or payments to unverified suppliers. Can everyone review the list and add any other red flags you've encountered? We also need to define clear escalation thresholds.",
            "mentions": [
              381305,
              505737,
              544735,
              554843
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 544735,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "The list in A4 is a good starting point. I'd add 'unusually high revenue figures right at the end of a reporting period'. I've seen that a few times. For escalation, maybe any single indicator over a certain monetary value, or a combination of three or more smaller indicators, should trigger a formal review?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "Excellent addition, I've added it to A4. Your threshold suggestion is smart - it combines impact and pattern detection. Let's refine that. How about: escalate if a single suspicious transaction is over €5,000, OR if we spot 3+ different indicators in the same file, regardless of value?",
            "mentions": [
              544735
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 554843,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "That sounds clear. Who do we escalate to? The accounting manager?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Correct. The guideline in A4 specifies a two-step process: first, flag it to the accounting manager. They will then decide if it needs to go to the compliance officer. This ensures we have a proper chain of review.",
            "mentions": [
              554843
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 381305,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "What if a client just makes a lot of mistakes? How do we know it's fraud?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 544735,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "That's the point of the indicators. We aren't deciding if it's fraud, we are just flagging patterns that are suspicious. The compliance officer makes the final call. Our job is to spot the signs.",
            "mentions": [
              381305
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 505737,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "The list looks ok.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "Okay, it seems we're aligned on the indicators and the escalation steps. I've updated A4 with everything. Let's make a formal decision to confirm this list and the escalation process.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Now, for T11, we need a simple way to log these incidents. I've created a template with fields for: Client ID (anonymised), Date Spotted, Indicator(s) Triggered, Brief Description, and Escalation Date. Does this cover what we need to track?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 544735,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Yes, that's perfect. Simple and has all the key info.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 554843,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Looks good. So we create an entry in this log every time we escalate?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Exactly. Every time the threshold is met and you notify the accounting manager, you create an entry. This gives us a clear record. Any objections to this format and process?",
            "mentions": [
              554843
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 381305,
